## Delivered: `RouteAnnouncer` Apple shared surface (P4 · 0002)

I built a production-polished, native SwiftUI parity of `web/src/components/a11y/RouteAnnouncer.tsx` — an invisible, polite VoiceOver route-change announcer — as 9 files under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/`, mirroring the established `misc-surfaces` architecture (Adapter / Model / View / Views / States / Previews / strings / Tests / ModelTests).

**Faithful web parity** (every source branch, no invented states):
- `useLocation` → P1/S8 `RouteSource` seam (no HTTP in the view); `document.title` → localized `route.<id>` title
- first-render suppression, empty-title → cleared region, and the `'\u200B'.repeat(counter % 4)` rotation so a repeated title still re-speaks
- 100 ms settle timer + `clearTimeout` cancellation via injectable seams; `aria-live="polite"` → `AccessibilityNotification.Announcement`
- its own dedicated region (not `useAnnouncer`) — exactly as the source documents. No loading/error/offline states because the source does no fetch (documented, not narrowed).
- P1/S10 i18n facade (no English literals), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, full VoiceOver labels.

